Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of signed and unsigned integer arithmetic in the timestamp adjustment calculations. Specifically, the use of a signed 64-bit variable (`s64 adjust`) in conjunction with an unsigned 64-bit variable (`u64 ns`) led to unintended behavior on 32-bit systems, where the compiler treated the addition as a `u64 + u32`, resulting in an off-by-error in the timestamp calculation. The adjustment logic was also inconsistent between the transmit and receive functions, further complicating the issue.

Here is the patch:

